s environment. If `is_default` is true, all the user's repositories use it, so what only one repository needs stays off it: move this session to an environment in `saved_for_session_repositories` with switch_environment and call this tool again (if none is `switchable_by_you`, propose nothing and tell the user which is saved for this repository and why this session cannot move to it), or, if the list is empty, propose a personal one with create_environment and `switch_session`. Edit the Default when every project would want the change, `session_has_repository` is false, or the list is empty and `switch_session` is not offered. A repo's setup script is never for the Default. In any other environment, edit when `editable_by_you` is true, whichever repository it was made for; otherwise propose a personal environment with create_environment, or tell the user the `not_editable_reason`. request_credential saves on the environment this session runs in. (5) Propose once and say why, with the evidence. If the user declines, do not propose a change for that need again in this session.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__get_environment", "schema": {"description": "Describe the cloud environment THIS session runs in, or, given `environment_id`, another environment the user can see (their own or one shared with their organization; ids come from list_environments). An environment is the saved setup a cloud session runs in: allowed network hosts, environment variables and a setup script. Returns its name and, for this session's own environment, its description; whether it is personal or shared with the organization; its network access (unrestricted, or the allowed hosts and whether package managers and MCP servers are allowed); the NAMES of its environment variables (values are never returned); its network secrets, if the user may edit it (host, header, name; never a value); whether it has a setup script (the script itself only when you could edit it); whether it is the environme